  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_034 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted) is the clear best at 0.706 accuracy. Across all comparisons, avgpool has outperformed transformer (e.g., 0.639 vs 0.573 with pca_n2000+resnet50), but that gap was measured with PCA embeddings. scvi_n200 produces learned, richer representations that may benefit more from attention-based (transformer) aggregation to selectively weight profile interactions. Question: Can transformer aggregation with the strongest encoder pair (scvi_n200 + vit_l) close or surpass the avgpool result? Why this experiment: It is the single most informative untested variation of the best configuration—only the aggregation method changes. If it beats 0.706, it meaningfully improves the final answer; if it does not, it confirms avgpool is optimal and the remaining experiment can be spent on a longer-shot alternative (e.g., singleprofile). Expected relative cost: moderate, roughly 7–9 GPU hours (transformer adds attention computation over avgpool's 4.82 h, but vit_l and scvi_n200 are already in the pipeline), which is acceptable given the high information value."
}

